   "evidence": "In-repo precedent for the sibling combination: `ChargeConjugation.lean:153` `def valenceNumber (f : Pdf (Species Flavor)) (i : Flavor) (Q2 : \u211d) : \u211d := mellinMoment f 0 (.quark i) Q2 - mellinMoment f 0 (.antiquark i) Q2`, with `valenceNumber_def` (156) and six downstream lemmas. `SumRules.lean:119` already names the quantity: \"`deltaU`, `deltaD`, `deltaS` are the scale-dependent quark helicity charges `\u0394q(Q\u00b2) = \u222b\u2080\u00b9 dx [\u0394q(x, Q\u00b2) + \u0394q\u0304(x, Q\u00b2)]`\".",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Polarized/PartonModel.lean",
   "fix": "Name it beside its sibling in `PDF/ChargeConjugation.lean`: `def helicityCharge (f : Pdf (Species Flavor)) (i : Flavor) (Q2 : \u211d) : \u211d := mellinMoment f 0 (.quark i) Q2 + mellinMoment f 0 (.antiquark i) Q2`, with a `helicityCharge_def` restatement, and state the three theorems above in terms of it, so the Ellis-Jaffe instance reads `EllisJaffeSumRule (partonModel LightFlavor.charge \u0394) (helicityCharge \u0394 .u) (helicityCharge \u0394 .d) (helicityCharge \u0394 .s) 0`.",
   "issue": "The helicity charge `mellinMoment \u0394 0 (.quark f) Q2 + mellinMoment \u0394 0 (.antiquark f) Q2` has no name: it is written out inline nine times, in `firstMomentG1_partonModel` (239), `firstMomentG1_partonModel_lightFlavor` (255-257) and both sides of `ellisJaffeSumRule_partonModel_iff` (284-288). Consumers of the iff must syntactically reproduce three explicit lambdas to instantiate `EllisJaffeSumRule`, whose own fields `deltaU deltaD deltaS : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` are precisely these functions.",
   "line": 239
  }
